# Part F: Installing Burp CA Certificate for HTTPS Interception

## Step 18: Export Burp CA Certificate

In Burp Suite:

1. Navigate to:

```text id="f1p6vz"
Proxy → Options
```

2. Click:

```text id="r5m9qd"
Import / Export CA Certificate
```

3. Select:

   ```text id="n2v8wx"
   Certificate in DER Format
   ```

4. Save file as:

```text id="k7t4pm"
burpcer.der
```

Save it in Downloads folder.

---

## Step 19: Push Certificate to Emulator

Open Command Prompt.

Navigate to platform-tools:

```bash id="p8w2vn"
cd C:\Users\Admin\AppData\Local\Android\Sdk\platform-tools
```

Push certificate:

```bash id="x4q7me"
adb push C:\Users\Admin\Downloads\burpcer.der /sdcard/Download/
```

Observation:

* Certificate transfers successfully to emulator.

---

## Step 20: Install Certificate in Emulator

Inside emulator:

1. Open:

   ```text id="m6t1zr"
   Settings
   ```

2. Navigate to:

```text id="j3v8pk"
Security & Privacy
→ More Security & Privacy
→ Encryption & Credentials
→ Install a Certificate
→ CA Certificate
```

3. Select:

   ```text id="u5x2rd"
   burpcer.der
   ```

4. Confirm installation.

Observation:

* Burp CA certificate installed successfully.

---

# Part G: Verifying HTTPS Interception

## Step 21: Open HTTPS Website

Inside emulator browser, visit:

```text id="c9w4qm"
https://example.com
```

---

## Step 22: Analyze HTTPS Traffic

In Burp Suite:

```text id="r7p1vx"
Proxy → HTTP History
```

Observation:

* HTTPS requests and responses become visible.
* Burp Suite successfully decrypts HTTPS traffic.

